{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>As the children of Esav did to me.</b> It is impossible to explain that it refers back to the nearby phrase ״תשבירני אוכל בכסף״ — 'sell me food for silver' — for it says ״והמואבים היושבים בער״, and it is known that the Moabites did not do so, for it is written (Deuteronomy 23:4–5): ״על דבר אשר לא קדמו אתכם בלחם ובמים״. Rather, it refers back to the word בדרך — 'on the way.' It says: 'as the children of Esav did to me' — that they gave me a way to pass through, for we circled Mount Seir on the way, in the manner of what is written: ״אתם עוברים בגבול אחיכם בני עשו״ and so forth. For the children of Esav wanted this — that they should pass through the way of their land; also their king, the king of Edom, wanted this, but he did not let them pass through the way of his domain, which was the short route to the Land of Israel. And this is the meaning of the king's words when he said (Numbers 20:18): ״לא תעבור בי״ — 'you shall not pass through me' — that is, through the way of my domain; but through the way of their land there was no prevention, neither from the side of the king nor from the side of the people. And there I have written it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:57.717784889Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}